Rast <rast2@hotmail.com> writes:
> > two invisible monsters hitting one another should not be visible
> 
> Shouldn't you be able to hear them, though?  If you can hear your invisible 
> dog fighting an invisible monster, you should be able to hear two invisible 
> monsters fighting each other.

Yes, you can. The fix changes messages about "It hits it." to "You
hear some noises."

> > treat handlessness as a major problem when deciding prayer outcome
> 
> So... the god will polymorph you back to your normal form?  Or what?

This is in response to the two-handed weapon problem; cursed items are
usually a minor problem, but cursed items that leave you without a
free hand are now a major problem. Nothing to do with polymorph.

> > perform artifact touch checks when putting on accessories
> 
> I thought it already did that.

It trapped W, but not P. Only affects the Eyes of Tapioca and the
Overworld. You noted this yourself during the last round of change
discussion, <MPG.18c5bf7a9f94d418989fdb@pnews.dmv.com>, and I reported
it.

> > missing noun in message when horns pierce through your helmet
> 
> Huh?

"You turn into a minotaur!  Your pierce through your fedora."

is now

"You turn into a minotaur!  Your horns pierce through your fedora."

as it should be.

> > the age of a potion of oil from a bones file wasn't being handled correctly
> 
> Huh?

The change of relative clocks from bones file to new game was being
treated correctly with regard to timed light sources for candles,
oil lamps, brass lanterns, candles, and the Candelabrum, but _not_
potions of oil; so they'd go out at the wrong time (or not at all).

> > is_damageable was using is_rottable incorrectly
> 
> What does that mean in-game?

No idea, to be honest. But it wasn't passing the function the
argument it should have mean, which would have meant the wrong
results.

> > don't allow polymorphed player to web over the stairs
> 
> Why not?

I suspect that hiding the stairs is considered too nasty for bones
files.

